<</Alt(Empirical data on the choruses of male Japanese tree frogs over a short time scale. \(a\) Photograph of a male Japanese tree frog. \(b\) Anti-phase synchronization of two frogs. \(c\) Tri-phase synchronization of three frogs. \(d\) Clustered anti-phase synchronization of three frogs. The male frogs tend to avoid call overlaps with each other over a short time scale. The data shown here are obtained from our previous study [12]. Refer to the image caption for details.)/K 4/P 1014 0 R /Pg 149 0 R /S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>
